<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.Africa might face fuel levy increase - paper.</title>
<headline>S.Africa might face fuel levy increase - paper.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>South African Transport Minister Mac Maharaj had accepted recommendations which might result in an increase in the fuel levy to cover the growing shortfall in the Road Accident Fund, Business Day newspaper reported on Thursday.</p>
<p>The report said that in terms of the recommendations, drawn up by special adviser Joel Joffe, the government might have to inject cash into the the fund to rein in its eight billion rand deficit, which is expected to grow by a further two billion rand per year if the system is not restructured.</p>
<p>He recommended that the government increase the fuel levy as it did not bring in enough money for half the benefits provided by the fund, which is intended to provide cover for victims of road accidents.</p>
<p>--Johannesburg newsroom -27-11-482.1003</p>
